    "q-122885": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122885",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/b00e13fc7b827b9c3960073679ee651f6bce5a6193e0b0af1907738691a287ed.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=1,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=3,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+3\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{12} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-122885-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"88\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msub><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45A TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>21</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
