    "q-122961": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122961",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/48356d566752c064e9381c2f9ce27ef12bbdd86a29a2dab0d3dda05088630006.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})+{m}_{41}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{41})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}+2{m}_{41}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/90ed44b97d085413780f2dce297dd78ffa4c968a244e73c431d2e9aa30e14d22.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/860ba8cf7e5135f7e2eedcde7534fe9880feb38c29163625e32b79f18fce2f2f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,3)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,3)=2 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,3)=1 \\\\ {m}_{41} & =f(4,3)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0=12.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
