    "q-122966": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122966",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/3be0ba3fa44ba61e0b55500e588387cd087b8d2f2687c5636c9b053f1f8dc5d6.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/9fa44875a37e8c7b7bc69b175ac1f30fe73af936565e68ecaa82e02b7617b330.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/595d13ca8ec18056038a855e96ca4a3d8cc967182dae5c54b9746c731238413b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,1)=6 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=6+1+5+0=12.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
