    "q-75230": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75230",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/9b26ea696afda59a7181f062c7c9fab4be373035678eafa0da51bf2b22f9f4b3.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13})+{m}_{23}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $6$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}+{m}_{13}+{m}_{23}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/70e4f9cd213e0dc4429e21cacf5c375d4def1e9ba021f05e45ee6e7820c5ff36.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224902/assets/8135011b8384a668d4bab28282220bb0560e1ae64c2f1d623822435349067f18.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=2 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{13} & =f(1,3)=4 \\\\ {m}_{23} & =f(2,3)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =2+3+3+4+4+5 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
